# ERP integration credentials — template. Copy to `.env.erp` and fill in.
#
#   cp backend/.env.erp.example backend/.env.erp
#
# `.env.erp` is gitignored. NOTHING real belongs in this file.
#
# You need NONE of these to work on ERP code. ~300 hermetic tests run with no
# credentials at all, and every live-system test skips with a reason naming the
# variable it wants:
#
#   cd backend && venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_erp_*.py -q -rs
#
# Fill in only the tier you are working on. See docs/erp/README.md.


# --- Odoo (Tier 3) — no credentials needed -----------------------------------
#
# Fully self-hosted. Nothing here is secret; the sandbox is disposable.
#
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.erp-sandbox.yml up -d
#   cd backend && venv/bin/python scripts/setup_odoo_sandbox.py
#
# Start here if you are new. It is the only connector validated end to end against
# a real server for free, and it exercises the machinery every connector shares.

RUN_ODOO_INTEGRATION=0          # set to 1 to enable the integration tests
# ODOO_URL=http://localhost:8169
# ODOO_DB=omniusgrid_test
# ODOO_USER=admin
# ODOO_PASSWORD=admin


# --- SAP S/4HANA (Tier 4) — free API key, issued instantly -------------------
#
# https://api.sap.com -> sign in -> profile -> API Key -> Show/Copy
#
# Issued to a PERSON, so it cannot be provisioned from CI. Get your own; do not
# borrow a colleague's.
#
# Exercises the $batch multipart parser against genuine SAP bytes — the one thing
# our own fixture cannot do, since the fixture encodes the same assumptions as the
# code it tests.

# SAP_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
# SAP_SANDBOX_SERVICE=API_PURCHASEORDER_PROCESS_SRV
# SAP_SANDBOX_ENTITY_SET=A_PurchaseOrder


# --- Dynamics 365 / Dataverse (Tier 4) — free Developer Plan -----------------
#
# Full walkthrough: docs/erp/dynamics-dataverse-setup.md  (~20 minutes)
#
# DATAVERSE_ORG is the SUBDOMAIN ONLY. For https://org1a2b3c4d.crm.dynamics.com it
# is `org1a2b3c4d` — not the URL. The connector builds
# https://{org}.api.crm.dynamics.com/api/data/v9.2/ itself.
#
# DATAVERSE_CLIENT_SECRET is the secret VALUE from Certificates & secrets, not the
# Secret ID in the next column. Entra ID's own error says so, which is how often
# people get it wrong.
#
# Run `venv/bin/python scripts/dynamics_verify.py` BEFORE the tests. The most common
# setup mistake — no application user — surfaces as
# `403 0x80072560 "The user is not a member of the organization."`, which says
# nothing about the actual cause. The script names it.

# DATAVERSE_ORG=
# DATAVERSE_TENANT_ID=
# DATAVERSE_CLIENT_ID=
# DATAVERSE_CLIENT_SECRET=


# --- Intuit QuickBooks Online (Tier 4) — free sandbox, one-time consent ------
#
# QuickBooks advertises NO client-credentials grant, so a client id and secret
# cannot mint a token on their own. A human must approve access to a company once:
#
#   export INTUIT_CLIENT_ID INTUIT_CLIENT_SECRET
#   cd backend && venv/bin/python scripts/intuit_authorize.py
#
# Register http://localhost:8399/callback as a redirect URI on the app first, or it
# fails AFTER sign-in. That cannot be pre-flighted: Intuit returns byte-identical
# sign-in pages for registered and unregistered redirect URIs.
#
# THE REFRESH TOKEN ROTATES. Intuit issues a new one on every refresh and retires
# the previous one, so this value goes stale as soon as anyone else uses it. Two
# people running the harness against the same company means the second gets
# `invalid_grant`. Use separate sandbox companies.

# INTUIT_CLIENT_ID=
# INTUIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# INTUIT_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# INTUIT_REALM_ID=
# INTUIT_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox


# --- NetSuite / Infor / Epicor — no free tier --------------------------------
#
# All three require account or partner approval, so they are covered by Tier 0/1
# only: static guarantees and request-shape assertions. If you obtain access,
# tools/erp-mocks/fetch-spec.sh knows the exact endpoint and Accept header for
# NetSuite's and Epicor's specs.

# NETSUITE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# NETSUITE_BEARER_TOKEN=
# EPICOR_BASE_URL=
# EPICOR_API_KEY=
